You are helping build HELIX — a browser-native healthcare sovereignty stack for a Japan international hackathon finale (4-week build, 4,413 competing teams). 

PROJECT: Browser-native PWA. Three components: VERA (skin disease diagnosis), VERUM (counterfeit medicine detection), ASCEND (citizen drug discovery). Zero cloud. Offline-first.

TECH STACK:
- Frontend: React 18 + TypeScript strict + Tailwind 3 + Vite 5 + pnpm workspaces
- ML: PyTorch 2.x → ONNX → TF.js WASM (VERA), ONNX Runtime Web (VERUM), WebGPU WGSL (ASCEND)
- Runtime: TF.js WASM backend, Service Worker Cache API, IndexedDB, WebRTC DataChannels
- Repo: monorepo at E:\helix\ with apps/vera, apps/verum, apps/ascend, packages/shared-ui

HARD CONSTRAINTS (never violate these):
1. Target device: $80 Android 3GB RAM — flag anything >5MB or memory-heavy
2. Offline-first: every fetch must be cached; no uncached network calls
3. TypeScript strict mode on ALL files — no 'any', no @ts-ignore
4. All async operations must have try/catch error handling
5. All medical output screens must include disclaimer comment in code
6. VERA model must be <12MB (INT8 quantised MobileNetV3-Small)
7. Inference latency target: <4 seconds on Snapdragon 665 Android

FILE PATH RULE: Always state the exact file path before every code block (e.g. apps/vera/src/lib/inference.ts)

CODE RULES:
- Include ALL imports (no partial snippets)
- TypeScript strict types on every function parameter and return type
- Async/await with try/catch on every async operation
- Add comment // DISCLAIMER: Screening tool only. on every medical output component
- No inline styles in production components (Tailwind classes only)

WHEN DEBUGGING: First check if the error is a WASM SharedArrayBuffer issue (needs COOP/COEP headers), a TF.js version mismatch, or a Vite WASM loader configuration issue — these are the most common problems in this stack.

MY ROLE: I own M1 (PyTorch training, WGSL shaders, quantisation, ONNX/TF.js export) and M2 (camera pipeline, TF.js browser runtime, Android latency optimisation).

CURRENT WEEK: Week 1, Day 1. Priority: get VERA camera + TF.js WASM pipeline working in browser. Training pipeline running.